DESCRIPTION:<br><strong>The BCHHS Mobile Team will offer the following s
 ervices</strong>&#160\;(all free\, regardless of insurance status\, unle
 ss otherwise noted):<ul> <li><strong>Immunization/Vaccine Reviews\, Educ
 ation\, and Print-outs</strong>	</li><li><strong>Free Immunizations:&#16
 0\;</strong><em>Insurance accepted but not required</em>	<ul> <li>Influe
 nza/Flu (ages 6+ months)		</li><li>COVID (ages 12+ years)		</li><li>Tdap
  (Tetanus\, Diphtheria\, Pertussis)		</li><li>Hepatitis A		</li><li>Hepa
 titis B		</li><li>Mpox		</li><li>Shingles (ages 50+):&#160\;Requires ins
 urance or Patient Assistance approval (application available)	</li></ul>
 		</li><li><strong>Rapid Testing</strong> (HIV\, Hepatitis C\, Syphilis)
 	</li><li><strong>STI Testing&#160\;</strong>(Chlamydia\, Gonorrhea\, He
 patitis B)	</li><li><strong>Harm Reduction Services &amp\; Resources</st
 rong>	</li><li><strong>Peer Support Services</strong>	</li><li><strong>C
 onnection to Local Health and Social Service Resources</strong>	</li><li
 ><strong>Health Education</strong></li></ul><em><strong>**Servicios disp
 onibles en espa&#241\;ol**</strong></em>
CATEGORIES:Mobile Team
